{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"willing-cellular-carp","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Split out of chewed-illicit-blacklemur (b8f7-65be-ec00-4844), which recorded two unrelated CI\nflakes together. That ticket fixes the bridge fsck snapshot oracle; this one is a distinct\ndefect with a different mechanism and a different fix, so it is tracked separately.\n\nTEST: tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py::\ntest_plan_review_sidecar_emit_two_clone_union (observed failing on ubuntu, py3.12)\n\nSIGNATURE: AssertionError: clones do not share a base\n\nMECHANISM: the failing assertion is a FIXTURE PRECONDITION, not the invariant under test. In\n_assert_emit_is_append_only, clone B is driven to sync by expiring its sync marker and then\nrunning an engine command whose pull is incidental:\n\n    _expire_sync_marker(tracker_b)\n    _engine_run(repo_b, \"list\")\n    base_a = _sidecar_paths(tracker_a, ticket_id, event_type)\n    assert base_a == _sidecar_paths(tracker_b, ticket_id, event_type), \"clones do not share a base\"\n\nWhen that incidental pull does not land A's pushed sidecar events, the test fails while\nestablishing its own setup. The append-only / reconvergence behaviour the test exists to prove\nis never reached, so a red here is not evidence of a product defect - it is a false alarm that\ncosts a Verified -1.\n\nSUGGESTED FIX: make the sync an explicit, asserted step rather than a side effect of\n_engine_run(repo_b, \"list\") - fetch/merge directly in the fixture and assert the expected\nsidecar set is present before proceeding. A setup failure should also be reported distinctly\nfrom an invariant failure so triage does not mistake one for the other.\n\nNote for whoever takes this: prefer a deterministic sync over a retry loop, and keep any\nassertions to ordering/content facts rather than timing budgets.","id":"1647-19b3-cbec-4a17","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"De-flake sidecar two-clone union fixture sync race"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786524209653245001,"uuid":"e944df76-b55d-4886-8c7c-91b13d7e6f00"}